# Netflix Content Intelligence Dashboard

## Project Overview

An interactive Power BI dashboard designed to analyze Netflix content data and generate clear business insights across content mix, genres, countries, audience maturity, original content, and growth trends.

The project transforms 10,000 content records into an interactive 4-page analytical dashboard using Power BI, Power Query, DAX, and data modeling.

## Key Objectives

- Analyze Movies vs TV Shows distribution
- Identify top genres and content-producing countries
- Understand content growth trends over time
- Analyze ratings and audience maturity
- Compare Original vs Non-Original content
- Enable interactive content exploration through slicers and filters

## Tools & Technologies

- Power BI – Dashboard development and business reporting
- Power Query – Data cleaning and transformation
- DAX – KPI and calculated measure development
- Data Modeling – Date Table and relationships
- CSV – Structured data source
- Data Visualization – Charts, KPI cards, slicers and interactive reports

## Dashboard Pages

### 1. Executive Overview
Provides a high-level view of total titles, Movies, TV Shows, Originals, Original %, growth trends, top genres and leading countries.

### 2. Content & Genre Analysis
Analyzes content by release year, ratings, maturity groups and genre categories.

### 3. Global & Audience Insights
Explores content distribution across countries, languages, ratings and Original content.

### 4. Catalog Explorer & Business Insights
Provides detailed content-level exploration along with business recommendations, project outcomes and challenges.

## Key DAX Measures

- Total Titles
- Movies
- TV Shows
- Originals
- Original %
- Movie %
- TV Show %
- Countries
- Genres
- Average Movie Runtime
- Average TV Seasons
- Previous Year Content
- YoY Growth %

## Key Insights

- Movies represent the larger share of the analyzed catalog.
- Content is distributed across multiple genres, countries and languages.
- The dashboard highlights differences in content maturity and ratings.
- Original and non-original content can be analyzed dynamically.
- Time-based analysis helps understand content addition and growth trends.

## Business Recommendations

- Prioritize high-performing genres and key markets for future content investment.
- Strengthen localized and original content strategies in high-potential markets.
- Optimize the Movie and TV Show mix based on catalog growth trends.
- Use ratings and maturity insights to support audience-focused content planning.
- Monitor content growth trends to support future acquisition and investment decisions.

## Project Outcome

Developed a 4-page interactive Power BI dashboard using 10,000 content records, featuring DAX-based KPIs, dynamic slicers, trend analysis, data modeling and detailed content exploration.

## Note

This project uses a synthetic, portfolio-ready Netflix-style dataset created for learning and demonstration purposes. It does not represent Netflix's official internal data.
